.TH batten-generate-schema 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-generate\-schema \- Emit the JSON Schema for a config or policy\-input surface, derived from the types that define it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten generate schema\fR [\fB\-\-surface\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Emit the JSON Schema for a config or policy\-input surface, derived from the types that define it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-surface\fR [default: authority]
Which surface to describe: the committed authority, the override layer, or a policy\-input document
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
authority: The committed authority: `batten.toml`
.IP \(bu 2
override: The raise\-only override layer: `batten.local.toml`
.IP \(bu 2
policy\-input: The `input` document a `scope = "tree"` Rego module reads
.IP \(bu 2
policy\-call: The `input` document a `scope = "mediated_call"` Rego module reads
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
